<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The House of Masks ~ Session 0.1 Actual Play

''The actual-play locus for Session 0.1'' of the campaign arc — ''Alpha Playtest: Caverns of
Neo-Thracia''. A flashback scene: the first meeting of the assembled company and the Lindwyrm,
played before the departure the the Salt-Stair booth (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/salt-stair-booth`) reports as already
underway. This locus holds the scaffold now — venue, cast, intent, the lifepath flows — and
receives the played record as the table generates it, in the witness pattern the shelf already
runs: operator turns as literal witness blocks, Lares turns verbatim, narrator segues marked
for later fleshing.

''One island of three.'' This locus serves the ''Actual-Play Lares'' — the event-voice island of
the Session 0.1 braid. Two sibling sessions run in parallel on their own causal islands: ''the
Referee's Second'' (prep, provisional-first) and ''the Painter of Words and Light'' (renders,
provisional-first). Text crosses islands only in human hands; arrivals read as
operator-introduced; the braid law rides at
`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/braided-islands` and the reds at
[[session-0-1-handoff-prompts|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/session-0-1-handoff-prompts]]. A session standing this locus
without its red still stands the braid.

''Player-safe by construction.'' The players sit at this table, so this locus carries rating
`ano` (the table's own collective record) and ''nothing rated `kapu` ever drafts here'' —
referee-side threads point at their own seats without content. The spoiler-boundary sits at the
draft, not the render, because the readers are the players.

''Timeline seat.'' This scene sits ''earlier on the worldline'' than the Salt-Stair booth. The
campaign present reads ''YOLD 5492'' (Elyncia_01 canon); the flashback's exact day and season stay
the operator's hand, so stamps ride Provisional witness until seated. No global now — the
flashback's stamp answers to its own log, not the booth's.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/venue>>

!! The Venue ~ The House of Masks

''The House of Masks'' — an intimate Dionysian cabaret main room with a large stage, seated within
a ''maze-like Inn'' near the main lifts — the magitech elevators — of ''High Delos'', one of the
primary sky islands. The Inn stands as the levitated House of Masks of old Delos's Theatre
Quarter: a maze-block merchant house — shops, workshops, and living quarters in one building —
its rooms floored with theatrical-mask mosaics. Under the late Empire this room hid an illegal
speakeasy, and when the Lindwyrm raised the holy sites in YOLD 5002 the whole house rode the
levitation up, cellar secrets intact. The cabaret's main floor keeps the masterwork the speakeasy
hid under boards through five centuries of Empire and flight: ''Dionysos in flowing oriental
garb, seated on a panther''. The old trade's bones remain in the architecture — the doors that
count their guests, the sightlines that favor the booths, the second way out of everywhere.
(Gaia's Delos holds the same house in ruin; the resonance crossed the void intact.)

''The levitation took the neighborhood whole'' — cellars, bones, smuggler-works and all; most of
the island surfaces around Delos rose the same day, and the Patroness surprised everyone. So the
speakeasy's Empire-cut works thread the underside of the sky-island like roots under a lifted
lawn — and the whisper-trade holds (the house neither confirms, denies, nor stops finding useful)
that the Masks control private lifts, passages, gates, pneumatic tubes, and other liminal ways:
to Low Delos, to the Docks, down past the lower layers into the dungeon wilds — and some say,
after the third cup, to nearby places in neighboring Nexuses. The rumors do half the security
work. The old low door by stage-left stays oiled, barred, and breathing sea-air at altitude.

''The management:'' Inn and Cabaret both run under the ''Order of Amaranth''. The room serves as
trusted neutral ground for meetings between the Order's agents, the Adventurer's Guild, the
Amorphous Dreams Cabal, ''the Lindwyrm herself-as-faction'', and the various guilds, companies,
cabals, and independent operators of the sky city. Neutral ground under a flower that never fades:
everyone knows whose floor it is, and that knowing keeps the peace better than any ward.

!!! The Genre Compass ~ four taverns, one braid

The room's tone braids four lineages, each contributing a law:

| Lineage | The law it contributes |
|---|---|
| ''Callahan's Place'' (Spider Robinson) | Shared pain is lessened, shared joy increased — the hospitality floor; puns as liturgy; the room heals sideways, never by interrogation |
| ''Tales From the Floating Vagabond'' | The door admits ANY genre and the bar absorbs it — gonzo arrivals normalized by staff who have seen stranger |
| ''The Vulgar Unicorn'' (Thieves' World) | Neutral-ground-with-knives — faction intrigue runs under every table; the peace holds BECAUSE everyone came armed and everyone knows it |
| ''The Draco Tavern'' (Niven) | Enormous things discussed calmly at small tables — the barkeep's-eye view; civilizational stakes at conversation volume |

The braid, stated once: ''a warm floor over deep water.'' The cabaret entertains genuinely, the
staff cares genuinely, the puns land genuinely — and the room also happens to hold, on any given
night, enough faction weight to tilt the sky island. Both truths stand; neither apologizes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/summit-week>>

!! The Summit Week ~ why the room is full

''The broadcast.'' Two months back, the Patroness sent word out to the other Nexuses — to the
Factions: an all-expenses-paid week's holiday at the House of Masks for any Factional
representative willing to hear an offer of contract with the Lindwyrm's partner company, ''the
Adventurer's Guild''. The representatives arrived this week. The cabaret's floor holds a summit
wearing a party.

''The missions fork.'' The player-daemon PCs carry the special sub-mission — Neo-Thracia. The
other Factions' representatives receive other missions; their tables, toasts, and quiet
negotiations dress the whole scene, and each rep in the room carries somewhere else to go.

''Aki came early.'' Four weeks before the summit: the first week touring the holy sites of High
Delos (and, by night, the vertical surfaces — chitin remembers what marble forgets), the next
three learning the new polyglot culture. By summit week she reads as the room's most acclimated
stranger.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cast>>

!! The Cast

''The house:''

* ''The local Lares instances'' — serving the patrons; the room's spirits know the regulars'
  cups and the strangers' tells. They speak in the house's manner: warm, exact, never anonymous.
* ''The faerie-folk staff'' — various fae; ''some deep agents of the Order'', others hired staff
  whose allegiance runs to the Order plain and shallow. Which are which stays a floor game the
  patrons lose politely.
* ''The patrons'' — the faction list above plus the public: guild tables, company crews, cabal
  couriers, lift-workers off shift, and whoever the maze admitted tonight.

''The principals:''

* ''Telarus, KSC'' — Arch-Sorcerer & Guru, Amorphous Dreams Cabal. Present in a private booth,
  ''waiting''. Pours before speaking, per his file.
* ''The Lindwyrm'' — ''yet to arrive.'' Humanoid dragon-kin form, ''mana-muting glamour on'' —
  the High Delos entrance, quiet where the Salt-Stair crossing flared the dish blue-white.
  A Great Dragon choosing to arrive at conversation-volume: the Draco Tavern law, worn as couture.

''The company (Alpha playtest PC + associated NPC cast):''

* ''Aki'' and ''Ichi'' (Freyja) — Lady Aki, wizard of the Shattered Isles, and Ichi, her
  construct-golem companion. Sheets near-final (the combat reconciliation stands enacted);
  Ichi seated with the booth party.
* ''The Gorgoness wave-jammer captain'' (Liv) — bard · swashbuckler · gunslinger; the paired
  rings that drink her serpent-spirit energy and fire it as bolts. ''Seated with Telarus, the
  PCs, and Ichi.'' Her ''gorgone(ss) crew'' holds a cluster of tables in the general audience —
  the ship drinks together.
* ''The prismatic elf'' (Kai) — kaiju-tracker / arcane-ranger out of the Shattered Isles'
  mushroom jungles and other chaotic-climate regions. Quiet, reserved; glowing prismatic
  ''softly'' as she enjoys the show — the glow answers the music before she would admit to.
  ''Patches the Grimalkin'' (Level 2,
  [[the-grimalkin|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/primary-characters/the-grimalkin]]) — her
  lynx-mount, fully geared for quick action — ''perches on the roof of the Inn, unnerving
  passers-by.'' Patches does not attend cabarets. Patches attends the exits.
* ''The ninja'' (Monty) — changeling-human youth, late twenties, and her ''Husky companion''.
  ''Both start offscreen.'' The entrance belongs to the table.
* ''Rhea the Moon Elf'' (Freyja's NPC, GM record) — Level 7 Combat-Rogue/Artificer, the
  Dragoness's intelligence-mistress; full notes at
  `lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/npcs/rhea-the-moon-elf` (@elyncia-referee). Her network's Neo-Thracian intel of the last
  two months underlies the summit's timing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/casting>>

!! Casting ~ the render sheet

//(Specification-grade appearance lines, carried verbatim from the heritage canon (FTLS Ch03) and
the character packages — V8.2 wants literal materials, colors, and light. Full workflow, sources,
and prompt anatomy: [[session-0-1-render-research|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/session-0-1-render-research]].)//

''Master style clause (verbatim, use whole):'' "orichalcum mythpunk: Bronze Age prestige lacquered
over strange telecom, divine engineering, and impossible logistics." Venue vocabulary: //salon ·
soirée · mirrored sky-dome · voidjammer lounge · crystal ballroom//. Render laws: awe-then-deflation
(compose grand, plant one precise mundane object) · deep time as fashion strata (décor layered like
the fresco-over-fresco walls) · ragged edges beat machine polish · no winking, ever.

''The floor and stage (staff & acts):''
* ''Faun host'' — "goat or deer legs, small curling horns, freckles like dappled sunlight; garlands
  of ivy, bells, or cork-wood pipes"
* ''Cat Lord management'' — "mythic cats with jewel-bright eyes, prehensile paws, and sometimes a
  serpent as a tail coiled like jewelry"
* ''Pixie waitstaff'' — "wings from dragonfly-glass to neon-etched gossamer; clothes stitched from
  leaves, circuitry, or salvaged glamour"
* ''Glow Kin stagehands'' — "soft glow along gills and freckles; cap-crowns like mantles; filament
  'hair'; spore halos in cold air"
* ''Bat Folk echo-singer'' (the torch act) — "slender bodies, oversized ears, dusk-coloured fur,
  eyes that catch stray gleams like polished stone"
* ''Porcelain Prince chorus line'' — "multiple identical bodies in porcelain masks and lacquered
  armor… visible cracks and kintsugi-style repairs that make them eerily beautiful" — one performer,
  many bodies, perfectly synchronized
* ''Frog Folk chorus'' — "pale mint to deep obsidian green… eyes reflect moonlight like still
  ponds… skin may pulse with bioluminescence during strong emotions"
* ''Spider Folk silk-aerialists'' — "human faces with ocular clusters shimmering like dew"
* ''Hobgoblin door-drill'' — "riotous colours, turning drill into festival"; lacquer masks
* ''Crystal Court goblin jugglers'' — "skin like tarnished copper or sea-glass; glitter-ink
  tattoos that rewrite themselves when nobody looks"

''The tables (patrons):''
* ''Elf salon-goers'' — "angular beauty, void-shadowed eyes, hair like moonlit ink or starlit fire"
* ''Spectrum Satrap emissaries'' — "bright-colored suits… glass helmets… skin and carapace shimmer
  from mother-of-pearl to oil-slick black; eyes like cut gems"
* ''Dragonborn envoys'' — "scales of chroma-sheen or hammered metal; ember eyes; some bear
  wing-stubs, some spined crests"
* ''Gorgonne crew'' — beautiful-Medusa faces, serpent braids dressed with
  coin-rings, small bronze wing-vestiges at the temples, smoked-glass gaze-spectacles
* ''Guild navigators'' (Melantha-pattern) — "black voidsilk, saffron braid, helm-link filaments;
  bronze-sun scales etched with tide formulae"; Ray-Bane status spectacles

''Principals:''
* ''Lady Aki'' — public glamour: "red and white shrine workwear; silksteel ritual robe layers;
  wide-brimmed ichimegasa with uchikatsugi-style veil; shrine bells, ofuda, spinneret tools, and
  soft faerie glamour." Palette: "red and white miko robes, purple outer cloth, iridescent chitin,
  orange mycelium glow, blue Ephyra glass." ''Honor the written negatives'' (concept-art package):
  no hypersexual framing, no generic witch hat, no modern sci-fi armor.
* ''Ichi'' — "hexagonal kikko-pattern plates of alchemically treated chitin — iridescent
  beetle-shell blues and greens… joins pulse with faint orange bioluminescent tracery"; open-faced
  sergeant's kabuto, "two glowing yellow-orange orbs"
* ''The Lindwyrm'' — public boards keep her ''deliberately impressionistic'' (witnesses disagree
  by canon); any render fixing her form routes through the operator first
* ''Telarus, KSC'' — ''no physical canon stands''; renders of him wait on the operator's hand
* ''Kai's prismatic elf · Monty's changeling · Patches the Grimalkin · the Husky'' — lifepaths
  open; render after their sheets close, not before

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/intent>>

!! Session Intent ~ character sheets by lifepath, co-narrated

''The work of Session 0.1:'' finish the character sheets for all player-daemon PCs and their
hallmark items / companions — ''in-fiction'', by talk-story. The method: a ''lifepath-life''
walk (the Central Casting flow-tradition, Jennell Jaquays) run as co-narration inside the scene:
each character's history unfolds AS cabaret — a conversation in the booth, a story told over the
rail, a number on the stage that turns out to be about someone in the audience. Operator input
rides as ''Joshu/Telarus''; the players speak their own; the Lares co-narrate and keep the room.

''Order of work:'' Ichi closes first with Freyja, then Aki; the others follow as the story calls
them up. The session's Gaia date: 2026-08-15 (provisional) — Boomtime, Bureaucracy 8, YOLD 3192.
The Elyncia stamp, thrown on the Discordian Oracle and riding Provisional until ratified:
''Prickle-Prickle, Bureaucracy 50, YOLD 5492''. Session omen (E-Jing throw, no changing lines):
''Hexagram 45 ~ Gathering Together'' — the table may re-throw live on the AppleKation.

''Mechanical anchors'' (verify at table, never assume):

* SDM Level 1 baselines per the Quickstart: Life 4 + 4/level · trait slots 7 + Thought ·
  item slots 7 + Strength · Defense 7 + ability + Skill + Ward · saves on Endurance/Aura.
* Aki L2 sheet stands reconciled; Ichi stands enacted (Life 12, THT-based defenses, flexible
  Inner Fire slots). Confirm at table; the sheets close here.
* The Gorgoness ''craft-sheet'' (the wave-jammer vessel) stands absent from the repo — this
  session births it or names its debt. The Vale river-rule verification waits on it.
* Kai's elf and Monty's ninja carry the most open lifepath: origins, capabilities, hallmarks —
  and the two companions (''the Cat'', ''the Husky'') seat as hallmark-companions with their
  own small statlines.

!!! The Lifepath Flows ~ per character, sketched

Each flow runs Central-Casting style — origin · shaping events · the turn · the reason-you-sail —
prompted in-scene, answered in-voice, written to the sheet as it lands:

* ''The Gorgoness captain:'' where the wave-jammer came from; how the crew chose her (or she
  them); what the rings cost and what they were before; why a bard's tongue in a gunslinger's
  holster. Her player's great-house airship history rides as resonance, never as script.
* ''The prismatic elf:'' the mushroom jungles and the chaotic-climate ranges; the first kaiju
  she tracked and the one she declines to speak of; where the prismatic glow entered the line;
  how the Cat adopted her (the direction of adoption stays hers to correct); why the deep dark
  under a Vale calls to a creature of wild light.
* ''The ninja:'' the gentlest flow at the table — a first-time player walks it. Changeling-human,
  late twenties, a Husky at her heel; the genre-bent Shadow seed (quiet blade, loyal dog, a past
  that arrives in fragments only when she chooses). The flow offers doors, never demands rooms:
  every prompt answerable with an image, a yes, or a pass.
* ''Aki & Ichi:'' closure pass — the lifepath already lived in play, and the ''origin now stands
  recorded'' on the sheets (the warding circle, the waking, the household born in one event). The
  session confirms the last blanks (hallmarks, bond-details, the grimoire's fresh rites) rather
  than re-walking it, and Ichi's road home runs toward the very Nexus his last host died fighting.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/format>>

!! Capture Format

The played record lands in this locus using the shelf's witness pattern
([[salt-stair-booth|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/campaign/salt-stair-booth]] sets the precedent):

* ''Operator/player turns'' — literal witness blocks, fenced, labeled by speaker; interpretive
  narrator segues above them, marked for later fleshing.
* ''Lares turns'' — verbatim as generated, frames whole.
* ''Witness stamps'' — `YOLD 5492` Provisional (day and season per the operator), per the no-global-now law; each stamp answers
  to its own log.
* ''Render path'' — the DreamDeck feed law
  (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/lindwyrm/dreamdeck-feed-architecture`) governs any later
  feed render; the cabaret's open floor maps to the open stratum, the private booth to `data`.
  Nothing here ever needs a kapu stratum — see #head.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open-forks>>

!! Open Forks (operator's + table's hands)

* ''The flashback's day and season'' — the oracle-thrown proposal rides the table: Bureaucracy 50,
  YOLD 5492, Provisional until ratified. Elyncia weekday names stay open beside it (canon shows
  ''Zaraday'' at YOLD 5002 — the Gaian five, or a local ring?).
* ''Monty's entrance'' — played live or narrated in; the flow holds both doors open.
* ''Patches and the Husky'' — hallmark-companion statline shape (one shared template, or two
  bespoke small sheets). Patches seats at Level 2; her voice and meeting-story stay Kai's to tell.
* ''The wave-jammer craft-sheet'' — born this session, or seated as a named debt.
* ''The arc's name'' — this locus and the Salt-Stair booth both stand flat on the shelf until
  the campaign-era arc earns its room and name.

